+    "title": "Studying any recommended prose or drama text: plot, character, setting and theme",
+    "body": "**Objectives:** apply a reusable method to any recommended prose text or play; summarise plot, describe characters with evidence, identify setting and state a theme with support.\n\n**Important status:** the school's recommended prose and drama texts are not identified in the supplied materials. The existing *The Gift of the Magi* and *The Proposal* lessons are labelled stand-ins. This lesson is a text-independent method. It does not replace the school's book and does not claim to cover it.\n\n**Teaching (method):**\n1. **Plot:** write five sentences — beginning, problem, rising events, turning point, result.\n2. **Characters:** pick two characters. For each, write one trait and one proof (an action or a line of speech). *A trait without proof is only an opinion.*\n3. **Setting:** state when and where it happens and how it affects events or mood.\n4. **Theme:** state the central idea as a sentence, such as “honesty costs something but is worth it”, and give one event that supports it.\n5. **Drama only:** list stage directions, dialogue and any change of scene; say how dialogue reveals character.\n\n**Worked example (original):** In a story where a boy returns a lost wallet at personal cost, *plot* = he finds the wallet; he is tempted; he returns it; the owner rewards him by offering friendship. *Character* = Ibrahim is honest (he walks two kilometres to return it). *Theme* = honesty is more valuable than money.\n\n**Practice:** choose your recommended text, or use the Study my text screen to paste a passage. Write the five plot sentences, one character with proof, the setting and one theme with support.\n\n**Answers / marking guide (10 marks):** plot in correct order 3, character with evidence 3, setting 2, theme with support 2. Reject a theme that is only a topic word such as “honesty”.\n\n**Assessment:** teacher marking from the learner's text. This tool does not establish that the intended text was studied.",
